      "Status": "Registered",
      "SummaryOfActivities": "We undertook systemic advocacy, providing expert advice, community consultation and policy analysis to make structural social change to policies and practices that improves the quality of life for LGBTIQA+ South Australians.   Our wins included advocating for a legislative ban on conversion practices, recruiting our inaugural CEO, supporting vulnerable LGBTIQA+ people to engage with the media to share their stories, connecting with South Australian councils through the Rainbow Council Network and representing LGBTIQA+ communities on key advisory bodies.  We built the capacity of LGBTIQA+ communities to actively participate in public life by providing opportunities for networking and connection. We supported LGBTIQA+ South Australians through the delivery of suicide prevention training, hosted events at Feast Festival, and were recognised for our work as winners of the South Australian Pride Awards  Sports Health and Wellbeing Award",
